nto the image plane. Classic vessel shape changes.\n\nLet's estimate the size. The field of view is 64mm. In slice 4, it's roughly 1/10th or 1/8th of the FOV. 64 / 10 is 6.4mm; 64 / 8 is 8 mm. Let's say 6mm. Okay.\n\n**Decision**\n\nVessel. The structure smoothly elongates and merges into a branching tubular network in the inferior slices, indicating it is a blood vessel turning into the axial plane rather than a discrete spherical nodule. 6 mm.\n\nLet's make sure the prompt requirements are met:\n*   Answer with one word, Nodule or Vessel.\n*   One short sentence of reasoning.\n*   Estimated diameter in mm.\n\nPerfect."
